I drive by a lot, and I see you here.

245
00:21:52,915 --> 00:21:54,917
I see a lot of people around you...

246
00:21:55,126 --> 00:21:58,211
...and I see these phones
and all this stuff on your desk...

247
00:21:58,420 --> 00:21:59,755
...and it means nothing.

248
00:22:00,005 --> 00:22:02,090
And when I came inside and met you...

249
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:05,051
...I saw in your eyes
and how you carried yourself...

250
00:22:05,301 --> 00:22:07,470
...that you're not a happy person.

251
00:22:08,095 --> 00:22:09,846
And I think you need something.

252
00:22:10,055 --> 00:22:12,932
If you wanna call it a friend,
you can call it that.

253
00:22:13,725 --> 00:22:16,018
You're gonna be my friend?

254
00:22:25,151 --> 00:22:26,653
What do you say?

255
00:22:30,822 --> 00:22:34,493
It's a little hard standing here
and asking you, so...

256
00:22:38,788 --> 00:22:42,457
Five minutes, that's all.
Just outside. Right around here.

257
00:22:42,665 --> 00:22:44,376
I'm there to protect you.

258
00:22:50,464 --> 00:22:52,716
Come on. Just take a little break.

259
00:22:55,635 --> 00:22:57,970
I have a break at 4:00.
If you're here--

260
00:22:58,221 --> 00:22:59,263
4:00 today?

261
00:23:00,430 --> 00:23:03,350
- I'll be here.
- I'm sure you will.

262
00:23:03,767 --> 00:23:06,478
- All right. Four p.m.
- Right.

263
00:23:07,061 --> 00:23:09,397
- Outside in the front?
- Yes.

264
00:23:10,106 --> 00:23:12,566
Oh, my name is Travis. Betsy?

265
00:23:15,985 --> 00:23:18,154
I appreciate this, Betsy.

266
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:35,085
<i>May 26th, four o'clock p.m.</i>

267
00:23:35,377 --> 00:23:39,214
<i>I took Betsy to Charles' Coffee Shop
on Columbus Circle.</i>

268
00:23:40,256 --> 00:23:44,844
<i>I had black coffee and apple pie
with a slice of melted yellow cheese.</i>

269
00:23:45,052 --> 00:23:47,303
<i>I think that was a good selection.</i>

270
00:23:47,512 --> 00:23:49,848
<i>Betsy had coffee
and a fruit salad dish.</i>

271
00:23:50,056 --> 00:23:51,975
<i>She could've had
anything she wanted.</i>

272
00:23:52,183 --> 00:23:54,893
15,000 volunteers
in New York alone isn't bad.

273
00:23:55,144 --> 00:23:56,937
But the organizational problems!

274
00:23:59,021 --> 00:24:02,066
Yeah, I know what you mean.
I got the same problems.

275
00:24:02,316 --> 00:24:07,362
I gotta get organized. Little things,
like my apartment, my possessions.

276
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:11,991
I should get a sign: "One of
these days, I'll get organiz-ized."

277
00:24:12,241 --> 00:24:13,868
You mean "organized"?

278
00:24:14,076 --> 00:24:15,953
Organiz-ized.

279
00:24:16,203 --> 00:24:18,621
Organiz-ized. It's a joke.

280
00:24:19,497 --> 00:24:22,083
O-R-G-A-N-E-Z-I-E-Z-D.

281
00:24:22,333 --> 00:24:26,587
You mean "organiz-ized." Like those
signs in offices that say, "Thimk."

282
00:24:32,758 --> 00:24:34,176
Do you like where you work?

283
00:24:35,595 --> 00:24:39,514
We've got some good people.
Palantine's got a good chance.

284
00:24:43,643 --> 00:24:45,728
You know you have beautiful eyes?

285
00:24:52,317 --> 00:24:54,402
Do you like the guy you work with?

286
00:24:54,652 --> 00:24:56,237
He's okay.

287
00:24:58,113 --> 00:24:59,489
But do you like him?

288
00:24:59,990 --> 00:25:04,452
He's funny and very good at his job.
Though he does have a few problems.

289
00:25:04,660 --> 00:25:06,829
I'd say he has quite a few problems.

290
00:25:08,581 --> 00:25:11,625
His energy seems to go
in the wrong places.

291
00:25:12,250 --> 00:25:15,045
When I walked in and I saw
you two sitting there...

292
00:25:15,253 --> 00:25:18,130
...I could just tell
that there was no connection...

293
00:25:18,339 --> 00:25:19,715
...whatsoever.

294
00:25:19,965 --> 00:25:23,176
And when I walked in,
there was something between us.

295
00:25:23,426 --> 00:25:26,095
There was an impulse
we were both following.

296
00:25:26,346 --> 00:25:29,015
So that gave me the right
to talk to you.

297
00:25:29,223 --> 00:25:32,976
Otherwise, I never would've
had the right to talk to you.

298
00:25:33,226 --> 00:25:36,187
I never would've had
the courage to talk to you.

299
00:25:37,104 --> 00:25:39,565
And with him,
I felt there was nothing.

300
00:25:39,774 --> 00:25:42,859
When I walked in, I knew I was right.
Did you feel that way?

301
00:25:46,446 --> 00:25:48,740
I wouldn't be here if I didn't.

302
00:25:51,075 --> 00:25:52,326
Where are you from?

303
00:25:53,118 --> 00:25:54,036
Upstate.

304
00:25:58,122 --> 00:25:59,749
That fellow, I don't like him.

305
00:25:59,957 --> 00:26:02,959
Not that I don't like him,
I just think he's silly.

306
00:26:05,420 --> 00:26:07,672
I don't think he respects you.

307
00:26:08,798 --> 00:26:11,926
I don't believe I've ever met
anyone quite like you.

308
00:26:23,268 --> 00:26:24,978
You wanna go to...

309
00:26:26,313 --> 00:26:27,980
...a movie with me?

310
00:26:28,523 --> 00:26:32,485
- I have to go back to work now.
- I don't mean now. Another time?

311
00:26:38,907 --> 00:26:41,450
Sure. You know what you remind me of?

312
00:26:42,368 --> 00:26:43,327
What?

313
00:26:43,577 --> 00:26:44,787
That song...

314
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:49,040
...by Kris Kristofferson.

315
00:26:51,668 --> 00:26:52,502
Who's that?

316
00:26:52,961 --> 00:26:54,628
The songwriter.

317
00:26:54,837 --> 00:26:56,380
"He's a prophet...

318
00:26:56,630 --> 00:26:58,340
He's a prophet and a pusher...

319
00:26:58,549 --> 00:27:02,593
...partly truth, partly fiction,
a walking contradiction."

320
00:27:04,262 --> 00:27:05,680
You saying that about me?

321
00:27:05,888 --> 00:27:07,597
Who else would I be talking about?

322
00:27:08,181 --> 00:27:09,891
I'm no pusher.
I've never pushed.

323
00:27:11,351 --> 00:27:13,811
Just the part about the contradictions.

324
00:27:14,061 --> 00:27:15,855
You are that.

325
00:27:46,463 --> 00:27:50,259
<i>I called Betsy again. She said
maybe we'd go to a movie...</i>

326
00:27:50,467 --> 00:27:53,386
<i>... after work tomorrow.
That's my day off.</i>

327
00:27:53,636 --> 00:27:57,765
<i>At first she hesitated,
but I called her again and she agreed.</i>

328
00:27:59,266 --> 00:28:00,934
<i>Betsy, Betsy. Oh, no.</i>

329
00:28:01,184 --> 00:28:03,854
<i>Betsy what?
I forgot to ask her last name.</i>

330
00:28:04,062 --> 00:28:07,356
<i>Damn! I gotta remember
stuff like that.</i>

331
00:28:18,490 --> 00:28:21,201
Don't worry about anyone
committing themselves...

332
00:28:21,410 --> 00:28:24,079
...until things come in
from California.

333
00:28:24,329 --> 00:28:27,206
Listen, I think we should've
waited for the limo.

334
00:28:27,457 --> 00:28:29,417
I don't mind the cab,
but I mind...

335
00:28:29,626 --> 00:28:33,045
...going to California
without the right preparation.

336
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:35,464
Are you Charles Palantine,
the candidate?

337
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:39,091
Yes, I am.

338
00:28:40,468 --> 00:28:45,388
I tell everybody that comes in this taxi
that they have to vote for you.

339
00:28:45,805 --> 00:28:47,182
Why, thank you...

340
00:28:49,267 --> 00:28:50,101
...Travis.

341
00:28:50,351 --> 00:28:53,437
I'm sure you'll win.
Everybody I know will vote for you.

342
00:28:53,646 --> 00:28:56,065
I was gonna put your sticker
in my taxi...

343
00:28:56,315 --> 00:28:59,192
...but the company said
it was against their policy.

344
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:01,027
They're a bunch of jerks.

345
00:29:01,235 --> 00:29:04,071
Let me tell you, I have learned
more about America...

346
00:29:04,279 --> 00:29:07,491
...from riding in cabs than in all
the limos in the U.S.

347
00:29:09,368 --> 00:29:12,203
- Oh, yeah?
- That's true.

348
00:29:12,703 --> 00:29:15,247
- Can I ask you something, Travis?
- Sure.

349
00:29:15,456 --> 00:29:18,625
What bugs you the most
about this country?

350
00:29:20,335 --> 00:29:25,130
Well, I don't know. I don't follow
political issues that closely, sir.

351
00:29:25,756 --> 00:29:27,841
Well, there must be something.

352
00:29:28,133 --> 00:29:32,220
Well, whatever it is, he should
clean up this city here...

353
00:29:32,428 --> 00:29:36,932
...because it's like an open sewer.
It's full of filth and scum.

354
00:29:37,391 --> 00:29:39,226
Sometimes I can hardly take it.

355
00:29:39,476 --> 00:29:42,436
Whatever becomes the President
should just...

356
00:29:43,145 --> 00:29:45,189
...really clean it up. You know?

357
00:29:45,439 --> 00:29:49,067
Sometimes I go out and I smell it.
I get headaches, it's so bad.

358
00:29:49,275 --> 00:29:52,362
And they just never go away, you know?

359
00:29:52,612 --> 00:29:54,948
I think that the President
should just...

360
00:29:55,447 --> 00:29:59,952
...clean up this mess. He should
flush it right down the fucking toilet.

361
00:30:08,041 --> 00:30:10,585
I think I know what you mean, Travis.

362
00:30:11,002 --> 00:30:12,838
But it's not gonna be easy.

363
00:30:13,046 --> 00:30:16,507
- We'll have to make radical changes.
- Damn straight.

364
00:30:18,175 --> 00:30:19,927
Here you go.
Keep the change.

365
00:30:20,136 --> 00:30:21,427
Thank you.

366
00:30:24,931 --> 00:30:26,975
- Nice talking to you.
- Nice talking to you.

367
00:30:27,225 --> 00:30:29,560
You're a good man.
I know you're gonna win.

368
00:30:29,935 --> 00:30:31,770
Thank you, I think.

369
00:30:54,455 --> 00:30:56,875
Just get me outta here,
all right?

370
00:31:00,294 --> 00:31:02,087
Come on!

371
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,590
Come on, baby.
This is a real drag.

372
00:31:04,840 --> 00:31:07,425
Now, come on!
Don't make a scene.

373
00:31:09,176 --> 00:31:10,511
You wanna get busted?

374
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:12,013
Bitch, be cool!

375
00:31:21,186 --> 00:31:22,980
Don't start no trouble.

376
00:31:24,315 --> 00:31:26,149
Cabbie, just forget about this.

377
00:31:26,608 --> 00:31:27,609
Be cool, bitch!

378
00:32:21,863 --> 00:32:23,782
Get your ass out of here!

379
00:33:32,756 --> 00:33:34,133
Hi there.

380
00:33:36,092 --> 00:33:38,719
- Have a nice day today?
- Not particularly.

381
00:33:38,928 --> 00:33:40,596
Got a present for you.

382
00:33:44,850 --> 00:33:48,519
Now back to Gene Krupa's
syncopated style shortly.

383
00:33:56,651 --> 00:33:57,902
Why'd you do that?

384
00:33:58,111 --> 00:34:01,030
What else am I gonna do
with my money?

385
00:34:01,405 --> 00:34:03,532
I wish you'd have listened to this.

386
00:34:04,116 --> 00:34:07,119
I would have, except my record
player doesn't work now.

387
00:34:07,369 --> 00:34:08,578
Your stereo's broken?

388
00:34:08,828 --> 00:34:11,247
How do you stand it?
I can't live without music.

389
00:34:11,497 --> 00:34:15,125
I don't follow music too much,
but I would really like to.

390
00:34:15,375 --> 00:34:17,919
Then you haven't played
this record yet.

391
00:34:19,671 --> 00:34:24,425
But I was thinking maybe we could
listen to it on your record player.

392
00:34:24,675 --> 00:34:28,344
Now, going back through
40 years of Chick Webb.

393
00:34:44,567 --> 00:34:46,110
You gotta be kidding.

394
00:34:46,319 --> 00:34:47,277
What?

395
00:34:47,485 --> 00:34:49,613
This is a dirty movie.

396
00:34:50,196 --> 00:34:54,033
No, no. This is a movie
that a lot of couples come to.

397
00:34:54,241 --> 00:34:58,162
- All kinds of couples go here.
- You sure about that?

398
00:34:58,871 --> 00:35:01,080
Yeah, I see them all the time.

399
00:35:04,375 --> 00:35:05,460
Come on.

400
00:35:47,912 --> 00:35:50,122
- Where are you going?
- I have to leave.

401
00:35:50,373 --> 00:35:52,624
- Why?
- I don't know why I came in here.

402
00:35:52,874 --> 00:35:55,126
- I don't like these movies.
- Well, I mean--

403
00:35:55,377 --> 00:35:58,253
I didn't know you'd feel
that way about this movie.

404
00:35:58,504 --> 00:36:01,382
- If I had--
- Are these the only movies you go to?

405
00:36:01,632 --> 00:36:04,592
Yeah, I mean I come and--
This is not so bad.

406
00:36:04,842 --> 00:36:08,638
Taking me here is as exciting
to me as saying, "Let's fuck."

407
00:36:13,100 --> 00:36:15,477
There are other movies
I can take you to.

408
00:36:15,685 --> 00:36:18,979
I don't know much about them,
but I can take you other places.

409
00:36:19,438 --> 00:36:20,981
We're just different.

410
00:36:21,524 --> 00:36:23,775
- Wait a second.
- I have to go.

411
00:36:23,983 --> 00:36:25,193
I've got to go now.

412
00:36:25,402 --> 00:36:29,030
- Wait a second, I want to talk.
- But I have to go.

413
00:36:29,656 --> 00:36:30,739
Taxi!

414
00:36:30,989 --> 00:36:35,244
Can I talk to you at least?
Won't you at least to talk to me?

415
00:36:35,494 --> 00:36:36,661
Take the record.

416
00:36:36,869 --> 00:36:39,205
- I've already got it.
- But, please.

417
00:36:39,455 --> 00:36:43,417
- I bought it for you, Betsy.
- Okay, now I've got two. Let's go.

418
00:36:43,625 --> 00:36:45,335
Can I call you?

419
00:36:46,545 --> 00:36:48,672
Jesus Christ, I got a taxi.

420
00:36:54,593 --> 00:36:56,136
Hello, Betsy.

421
00:36:56,344 --> 00:36:58,054
Hi, it's Travis.

422
00:36:59,931 --> 00:37:02,891
Listen, I'm sorry
about the other night.

423
00:37:03,142 --> 00:37:06,186
I didn't know that was
the way you felt about it.

424
00:37:08,063 --> 00:37:13,067
Well, I didn't know. If I--
I'd have taken you somewhere else.

425
00:37:14,318 --> 00:37:16,403
Are you feeling better or...?

426
00:37:17,320 --> 00:37:20,991
Maybe you had a virus or something.
A 24-hour virus, you know.

427
00:37:21,241 --> 00:37:23,492
It can happen. Yeah.

428
00:37:28,247 --> 00:37:30,790
You've been working hard, huh?

429
00:37:34,836 --> 00:37:38,130
Would you like to have
some dinner with me...

430
00:37:38,380 --> 00:37:41,008
...in the next few days or something?

431
00:37:44,010 --> 00:37:45,636
How about a cup of coffee?

432
00:37:45,887 --> 00:37:49,973
I could come by the headquarters
or something, and we could...

433
00:37:50,849 --> 00:37:52,684
Okay, okay.

434
00:37:55,269 --> 00:37:57,897
Did you get my flowers and the...?

435
00:37:59,815 --> 00:38:04,152
You didn't get them?
But I sent some flowers.

436
00:38:10,574 --> 00:38:12,701
Can I call you again?

437
00:38:13,118 --> 00:38:15,202
Tomorrow or the next day?

438
00:38:15,828 --> 00:38:18,748
No, I'm gonna--
Okay, yeah, sure.

439
00:38:19,040 --> 00:38:20,415
So long.

440
00:38:22,792 --> 00:38:25,003
<i>I tried several times to call her...</i>

441
00:38:25,253 --> 00:38:28,756
<i>... but after the first call,
she wouldn't come to the phone.</i>

442
00:38:29,214 --> 00:38:31,592
<i>I also sent flowers,
but with no luck.</i>

443
00:38:31,926 --> 00:38:34,427
<i>The smell of the flowers
made me sicker.</i>

444
00:38:34,677 --> 00:38:39,182
<i>The headaches got worse.
I think I got stomach cancer.</i>

445
00:38:39,806 --> 00:38:41,892
<i>I shouldn't complain, though.</i>

446
00:38:42,392 --> 00:38:44,394
<i>You're only as healthy...</i>

447
00:38:45,270 --> 00:38:47,730
<i>You're only as healthy as you feel.</i>

448
00:38:49,065 --> 00:38:50,441
<i>You're only...</i>

449
00:38:50,691 --> 00:38:52,360
<i>... as healthy...</i>

450
00:38:52,610 --> 00:38:53,985
<i>... as...</i>

451
00:38:54,235 --> 00:38:55,779
<i>... you...</i>

452
00:38:56,029 --> 00:38:57,364
<i>... feel.</i>

453
00:39:07,747 --> 00:39:11,334
- Let's not have trouble.
- Why won't you talk to me?

454
00:39:11,542 --> 00:39:14,002
You think I don't know you're here?

455
00:39:14,252 --> 00:39:16,254
You think I don't know?

456
00:39:16,463 --> 00:39:18,131
- Please leave.
- Take your hands off!

457
00:39:18,340 --> 00:39:20,508
I just want you to know--

458
00:39:20,716 --> 00:39:23,803
Please.
This is no place to do this.

459
00:39:24,595 --> 00:39:26,346
- Take your hands off!
- Just leave.

460
00:39:26,596 --> 00:39:29,891
- All right, leave, then!
- I wanna tell you...

461
00:39:30,141 --> 00:39:32,518
...you're in hell!
And you'll die in hell.

462
00:39:32,726 --> 00:39:35,479
- There's a cop over there.
- You're like the rest of them.

463
00:39:35,729 --> 00:39:38,022
Look, I'm calling the cop.
Officer!

464
00:39:40,983 --> 00:39:42,402
Officer!

465
00:39:44,028 --> 00:39:47,364
Don't come around here,
because I'll call the police!

466
00:39:48,407 --> 00:39:53,411
<i>I realize now, how much she's just
like the others, cold and distant.</i>

467
00:39:53,619 --> 00:39:55,287
<i>Many people are like that.</i>

468
00:39:55,496 --> 00:39:58,790
<i>Women for sure.
They're like a union.</i>

469
00:40:00,083 --> 00:40:01,543
Yo, cabbie!

470
00:40:09,341 --> 00:40:13,219
Pull over to the curb over there.
Right over there.

471
00:40:15,221 --> 00:40:16,055
No, don't.

472
00:40:17,472 --> 00:40:19,891
The fucking meter.
What are you doing?

473
00:40:20,267 --> 00:40:22,144
What are you doing with the meter?

474
00:40:22,352 --> 00:40:25,521
Did I tell you to do that
with the meter?

475
00:40:25,729 --> 00:40:29,608
Put the meter back.
I don't care what I have to pay.

476
00:40:29,858 --> 00:40:33,486
I'm not getting out.
Put the meter back on.

477
00:40:33,736 --> 00:40:34,696
Put it down.

478
00:40:36,114 --> 00:40:37,030
That's right.

479
00:40:37,281 --> 00:40:39,074
Put it down!

480
00:40:40,826 --> 00:40:42,202
That's right.

481
00:40:43,077 --> 00:40:45,580
Why are you writing?
Don't write!

482
00:40:45,788 --> 00:40:47,290
Put the thing down.
Just sit.

483
00:40:50,792 --> 00:40:53,879
I didn't tell you to write.
I just said, "Pull over."

484
00:40:54,129 --> 00:40:56,589
Pull over to the curb and sit here.

485
00:40:58,674 --> 00:41:00,134
We're gonna sit.

486
00:41:18,858 --> 00:41:22,861
Cabbie, you see that light up there?
